#!   DESCRIPTION="&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Purpose &amp;amp; Objectives&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;This workspace generates a dataset for an indoor scenario, either a living room or a kitchen, for displaying in augmented reality using the FME Realize app. User parameters, including contextual dependent parameters, are used to set the styling of the Revit features displayed in AR when running the app. &lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Transformers&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Clipper: Clips the Revit dataset to a selected room&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;AppearanceSetter: Sets appearance style(s) onto the sides of geometry surfaces &lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;RasterGeoreferencer: Sets the size of the texture to 1 by 1 m for applying as furniture upholstery&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data Source(s) - Reader Feature Type&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Autodesk Revit Reader reads in Revit elements, including living room or kitchen surfaces and furniture&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;OBJ Reader reads in plumbing features, in the Wavefront Obj format, as 3D models&#10;Autodesk 3ds Reader reads in 3D geometry of kitchen appliance data in 3ds format &lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data Output - Writer Feature Type&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;FME AR Writer saves the geometry into a form that is overlaid on a live view in AR&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Customization&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;To customize this workspace, you can change the following:&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;ul&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;Feature appearance (style, colour, texture) with the AppearanceSetter transformers&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;Attributes to display in AR as summary annotations with the AttributeCreator transformers&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;3D model data sources&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;/ul&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;If you&apos;re recreating this workspace with your own data, it is recommended to build the workspace from scratch as your dataset will have different attributes and schema (structure).&lt;/p&gt;"
