#! <COMMENT
#!   IDENTIFIER="200"
#!   COMMENT_VALUE="&lt;!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC &quot;-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.0//EN&quot; &quot;http://www.w3.org/TR/REC-html40/strict.dtd&quot;&gt;&#10;&lt;html&gt;&lt;head&gt;&lt;meta name=&quot;qrichtext&quot; content=&quot;1&quot; /&gt;&lt;meta charset=&quot;utf-8&quot; /&gt;&lt;style type=&quot;text/css&quot;&gt;&#10;p, li { white-space: pre-wrap; }&#10;hr { height: 1px; border-width: 0; }&#10;li.unchecked::marker { content: &quot;\2610&quot;; }&#10;li.checked::marker { content: &quot;\2612&quot;; }&#10;&lt;/style&gt;&lt;/head&gt;&lt;body style=&quot; font-family:&apos;Segoe UI&apos;; font-size:6pt; font-weight:400; font-style:normal;&quot;&gt;&#10;&lt;p style=&quot; margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-size:9pt;&quot;&gt;The user will see a room - depending on their choice, either a kitchen or a living room. It is recommended to &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p style=&quot; margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-size:9pt;&quot;&gt;explore the scene in a room with enough open space so that the augmented features do not interfere with real ones, and to avoid the risk of hitting real objects hidden behind augmentation.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/body&gt;&lt;/html&gt;"
